[[772,305,"the evidence suggested that the outcome of a transthoracic echocardiogram performed in January 2025 at the North Middlesex University Hospital was not reviewed by any clinician until May 2025","delayed review of echocardiogram result",""],[773,305,"appears to be no system in place to ensure that a result such as this is viewed and considered by a member of a relevant clinical team in a timely manner,","lack of result review system",""],[774,305,"no relevant pathway for the echocardiography team to flag a result such as this to the clinical team","absence of flagging pathway for critical results",""],[775,305,"the Hospital's own Mortality Review highlighted a number of learning points, I was not told of any action which has been taken in response to those matters as yet","lack of response to learning points",""],[2097,808,"The lack of CT scanning prior to hysterectomy, with reliance only on ultrasonography, raises the concern that the diagnosis of uterine sarcoma could be missed in the future and consideration should be given as to whether steps can be taken to address this risk.","missed uterine sarcoma diagnosis",""],[2196,852,"widespread communication issues","lack of communication between ward staff and medical staff",""],[2197,852,"lack of professional curiosity on the part of some staff members","skills knowledge deficit",""]]